A||||2||86SE||FireBall Exhaust:  Spark kills the engine.....||||8||
Z||000000||86SE||07-28-2000||06:48 PM||||I started my fire ball exhaust project today.  I taped into all 4 wires that go to the coil and pluged them in to a separate coil.  Then I hooked a spark plug to one end of a wire then hooked the other end to the coil.  Started the engine, grabbed the plug and touched it to the chassis......the engine died.  Started it again, put the plug about 1/4" away from the chassis, and it sparked fine without dragging down the engine too much.<P>The sparkplug has to be screwed into the tail pipe for it to shot flames out the back, but if it touches the ground the engine dies!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>So far I have taken off the 2 wires on the coil that face the front, no difference.  THen I pluged them back in, then disconnected the 2 wires that face the rear, no difference.<P>Any ideas why the second coil is 'sucking up' all the juice and killing the engine??  I really want fireball exhaust!!<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||8
Z||000001||84 Indy||07-29-2000||12:43 AM||||<BR>Try using an old distributer peferably something that does not requier a expensive module connect to a 12 volt motor and a coil for each tailpipe . If i remember you have to run the motor rich and i don't think it will work if you have a working cat of the car because the cat will burn your extra fuel . AND PLEASE BE VERY CAREFUL YOU DON'T WANT TO HURT YOUR CAR OR WORSE YOURSELF||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||07-29-2000||02:26 AM||||also the catalytic converter will be ruined if you run to rich for a certain length of time.   ||||reg||1
